 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Nvidia isn't the only chip company in search of more firepower.

 Intel yesterday upsized a previously announced common stock offering to $20 billion from $15 billion, and priced it at $95 per share. Proceeds are for "general corporate purposes" that may include "capital expenditures and working capital." Intel shares fell over 4% on the news. 
 
